  "summary": "An external actor at 40.80.148.42 broadly scanned imreallynotbatman.com for common web vulnerabilities, then focused on a discovered Joomla installation, alternating between path-traversal attempts to read local files and time-based blind SQL injection against the search component -- consistent with an attacker trying to confirm and weaponize a foothold in the public-facing web application, though this evidence set shows only the probing/exploitation attempts and does not establish that file disclosure or database access actually succeeded. A separate set of findings (anonymous SMB/Kerberos logons and Splunk-named process launches on we8105desk) occurred roughly 40 minutes earlier on an unrelated host and lacks any corroborating link (e.g., a shared source IP) to this web attack, so it has been left out of this chain rather than forced into the narrative.",
