  "benign_explanation_considered": "The strongest innocent explanation is that this traffic is an automated vulnerability scanner or authorized penetration test rather than a genuine attacker, since none of the responses in this evidence set confirm actual file disclosure or SQL result leakage. This is only partly ruled out: the requests show a single IP escalating sleep values in a controlled, iterative way and pivoting from generic probes to a specific, previously-discovered Joomla search endpoint over several minutes, a pattern more consistent with manual/semi-automated exploitation confirmation than with a benign crawler or scanner sweep, but the absence of confirmed data exfiltration in these logs means compromise itself remains unproven."
